Drawing an HTML / EPUB page honors the render's abort cookie.

htdoc_run_page() / epub_run_page() got a cookie but fz_draw_html() took none,
so an aborted render (the page scrolled away, the document closed) drew the
whole page anyway. fz_draw_html() takes the cookie and draw_box() stops
the walk when it's aborted, like reaching the restart place.
fz_draw_restarted_html() keeps its signature. (Idea from Vira Reader's
mupdf-html-cancellation.patch.)

